 "description": "Use when the user needs a bounded fit judgment about whether a specific finished footwear product is likely to work for a specific person in a stated use context, including pressure, toe contact, heel slip, width/size questions, dynamic-use problems, keep/exchange decisions, and fit-driven alternatives. Do not use for generic shoe education, style advice, simple size conversion, or medical diagnosis/treatment. When presenting a returned fit judgment, preserve the tool's decision, unknowns, next steps, alternatives, professional boundary, evidence state, and execution provenance. When coreJudgment is present, preserve its primaryState, reasonCodes, criticalUnknownIds, Case/Rule Set identity, and do not replace them with stronger host conclusions. Do not add or strengthen unverified product facts, gait or biomechanical labels, medical causal explanations or diagnoses, or extra size/width/lacing/product prescriptions unless they were independently established as verified evidence in the request. Keep any separately sourced external information clearly separate from the bounded fit judgment.",
